Hi there,

A quick question. I've been using RPostgreSQL for a while now and I think
it's great. But I wondered if it was possible to do something like this?

result <- dbGetQuery(con, 'myquery.sql')

What I mean by this, is instead of writing the SQL statement, can R fetch
the SQL code from out of a file instead? I ask this because I typically do
my SQL development using PgAdminIII, which I then save, and then copy and
paste the SQL code into an R script. This would save me some time if I
could just reference the SQL code itself.

Thanks

James

